{"title":"Workshop FH Hof / Münchberg April 2014","description":"Classes that Michael Zöllner teaches. See http://ixd-hof.de/","path":"intro-workshop-april-2014","grid_cols":200,"grid_rows":9,"cell_width":420,"cell_height":315,"css_class_name":"set-53495cdd6d303479634e0000","published":false,"id":"53495d696d303479634f0000","poster":null,"cells":[{"title":"\"Improv tech\" subtext","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"William Forsythe \"Improvisation Technology\" (1999) <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/user/GrandpaSafari/videos\" target=\"_blank\">on YouTube</a> and <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/William-Forsythe-Improvisation-Technologies-Analytical/dp/3775721843\" target=\"_blank\">DVD</a>"},"id":"53495f236d3034795d3a0000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":5,"y":7,"width":6,"height":1},{"title":"Improvisation Technology on YT","description":"","type":"iframe","additional_fields":{"iframe-src":"//www.youtube.com/embed/wUxRO9Jy8Rk","autoload":"1","attr-allowfullscreen":"allowfullscreen"},"id":"53495f8f6d303479604d0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/full/Screen_Shot_2014-04-12_at_5.49.05_PM.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/small/Screen_Shot_2014-04-12_at_5.49.05_PM.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/medium/Screen_Shot_2014-04-12_at_5.49.05_PM.png"}},"x":5,"y":1,"width":6,"height":6},{"title":"Synchronous Objects","description":"","type":"iframe","additional_fields":{"iframe-src":"//www.youtube.com/embed/uQdZBOVYLdI","autoload":"1","iframe-src-alt":"//www.youtube.com/embed/v2REtWg6-bo","attr-allowfullscreen":"allowfullscreen"},"id":"5349636a6d30347963510000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/full/Screen_Shot_2014-04-12_at_5.56.05_PM.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/small/Screen_Shot_2014-04-12_at_5.56.05_PM.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/medium/Screen_Shot_2014-04-12_at_5.56.05_PM.png"}},"x":12,"y":1,"width":6,"height":6},{"title":"Sync O subtext","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"Ohio State University (2009, Forsythe, Palazzi, Zuniga-Shaw) <a href=\"http://synchronousobjects.osu.edu/\" target=\"_blank\">\"Synchronous Objects\"</a>: what else might dance look like?<br />Also see the <a href=\"http://synchronousobjects.osu.edu/tools/counterpointTool.html\" target=\"_blank\">Counterpoint tool</a>"},"id":"534963c56d303479665d0000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":12,"y":7,"width":6,"height":1},{"title":"Deborah Hay explaining her way of dancing","description":"","type":"vimeo","additional_fields":{"vimeo-id":"91796020","autoload":"0","solo":"-1","attr-allowfullscreen":"allowfullscreen"},"id":"534966cf6d30347966600000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/full/Screen_Shot_2014-04-12_at_6.12.16_PM.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/small/Screen_Shot_2014-04-12_at_6.12.16_PM.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/medium/Screen_Shot_2014-04-12_at_6.12.16_PM.png"}},"x":26,"y":1,"width":6,"height":6},{"title":"Deborah explains subtext","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"Dancer and choreographer <a href=\"http://deborahhay.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deborah Hay</a>"},"id":"534967106d30347966610000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":26,"y":7,"width":6,"height":1},{"title":"Guest choreographers","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>Motion Bank Phase 1 (2010-2013)</h1><br/><h1><a href=\"http://scores.motionbank.org/dh/\">Deborah Hay</a><br/><a href=\"http://scores.motionbank.org/jbmf/\">Jonathan Burrows & Matteo Fargion</a><br/><a href=\"http://scores.motionbank.org/two/\">Bebe Miller and Thomas Hauert</a></h1><p>&nbsp;</p><p>William Forsythe chose these <b>guest choreographers</b> because their practice is different to his own hoping this would challenge the approaches and thinking developed so far.</p><br/><p>See our <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/60560235\" target=\"_blank\">2012 trailer</a> and <a href=\"http://motionbank.org/\" target=\"_blank\">phase 1 documentation website</a></p>"},"id":"534987396d30347963520000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":20,"y":1,"width":4,"height":7},{"title":"Intro text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>Introduction to Motion Bank project and material</h1><br/><p><a href=\"http://ixd-hof.de/\" target=\"_blank\">FH Hof / Münchberg, 2014-04-16</a></p></br><h2><a href=\"https://twitter.com/motionbank\" target=\"_blank\">@motionbank</a></h2><h2><a href=\"mailto:florian@motionbank.org\">florian@motionbank.org</a></h2>"},"id":"53498a966d30347966620000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":1,"y":1,"width":3,"height":7},{"title":"Score text with notes","description":"","type":"iframe","additional_fields":{"iframe-src":"https://lab.motionbank.org/dhay/text/score-text-notes.html"},"id":"53498b056d30347966630000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/screen-shot-2013-05-18-at-9.39.08-am-3.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/screen-shot-2013-05-18-at-9.39.08-am-3.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/screen-shot-2013-05-18-at-9.39.08-am-3.png"}},"x":45,"y":1,"width":3,"height":7},{"title":"Ros Warby performing \"No Time To Fly\" in Frankfurt, April 2011 (D02T02)","description":"This recording shows Ros Warby performing the solo \"No Time To Fly\".","type":"recording","additional_fields":{"xxx-recording":"D02T02","xxx-videoId":"247","xxx-content-url":"modules/flowplayer/index.html","xxx-file-name":"D02T02_Ros_sync_AJA_1","iframe-src":"/dh/dhay/player/?rec=D02T02&vid=69386&file=D02T02_Ros_sync_AJA_1&gid=24&perf=roswarby","autoload":"0","solo":"24","attr-allowfullscreen":"allowfullscreen","attr-mozallowfullscreen":"mozallowfullscreen","attr-webkitallowfullscreen":"webkitallowfullscreen","class":"hide-description"},"id":"53498b546d30347960500000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/record-5a-1.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/record-5a-1.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/record-5a-1.jpg"}},"x":55,"y":1,"width":9,"height":7},{"title":"Language title","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>Language</h1><p>The score for \"No Time To Fly\" has 4 different text types: <b>tools</b>, <b>images</b>, <b>instructions</b> and <b>notes</b>.</p>"},"id":"53498bb86d30347960510000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":49,"y":1,"width":4,"height":2},{"title":"Lang tool","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>What if the question “What if where I am is what I need?” is not about what I need but an opportunity to remember the question “What if where I am is what I need?”?</h1>"},"id":"53498db26d30347960520000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":49,"y":3,"width":5,"height":2},{"title":"Lang text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"In the score text to the left tab 2 has three <b>tools</b> (or questions), tab 16 has <b>images</b> (\"mall\", \"object\"), tab 7 has an <b>instruction</b> (the curve) and tab 3 has <b>notes</b> (normally prepended with \"Note:\")."},"id":"53498f1d6d30347963530000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":49,"y":5,"width":4,"height":2},{"title":"No Time To Fly text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>The solo \"No Time To Fly\"</h1><p>Deborah Hay arrived with a solo she wrote and performed herself in 2010. It was sent to the three dancers <b>Jeanine Durning</b>, <b>Ros Warby</b> and <b>Juliette Mapp</b> to be learned from the text only. In April 2011 the three arrived in Frankfurt one after the other and each performed the solo 7 times.</p>"},"id":"534993946d30347963540000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":39,"y":1,"width":4,"height":7},{"title":"The system text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>A system, based on the text?</h1><p><em>The performer who adapts one of my solo works calls into action 3 parallel roles: the dancer, choreographer, and the <b>executant</b>. Executant means <b>“putting into effect the exact demands”</b> which underlie the practice of performance of my movement material. Each dancer must be a conscious executant. At the same time the virtues of “fidelity and sympathy” with my choreographic preferences has to be felt.</em> – <a href=\"http://www.deborahhay.com/about.html\">Deborah Hay, SPCP</a></p>"},"id":"534a28366d30347966640000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":66,"y":1,"width":5,"height":3},{"title":"The score text is not the choreography without the tools","description":"","type":"vimeo","additional_fields":{"vimeo-id":"66955536","class":"hide-description"},"id":"534a412a6d30347963550000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/vimeo-66955536-438872257-640-3.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/vimeo-66955536-438872257-640-3.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/vimeo-66955536-438872257-640-3.jpg"}},"x":66,"y":4,"width":5,"height":4},{"title":"Raise interest","description":"","type":"vimeo","additional_fields":{"vimeo-id":"66955659"},"id":"534a51fd6d3034795d3e0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/vimeo-66955659-438634303-640-2.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/vimeo-66955659-438634303-640-2.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/vimeo-66955659-438634303-640-2.jpg"}},"x":75,"y":1,"width":3,"height":2},{"title":"Continuity to allow discontinuity","description":"","type":"vimeo","additional_fields":{"vimeo-id":"66955512"},"id":"534a525a6d30347963560000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/vimeo-66955512-438873188-640-1.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/vimeo-66955512-438873188-640-1.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/vimeo-66955512-438873188-640-1.jpg"}},"x":75,"y":4,"width":3,"height":2},{"title":"Disrupt linearity","description":"","type":"vimeo","additional_fields":{"vimeo-id":"67228548"},"id":"534a533e6d30347963570000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/vimeo-67228548-439121999-640.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/vimeo-67228548-439121999-640.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/vimeo-67228548-439121999-640.jpg"}},"x":78,"y":4,"width":3,"height":2},{"title":"Linearity","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>Tools and linearity and discontinuity</h1>"},"id":"534a53bd6d30347966660000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":72,"y":4,"width":3,"height":2},{"title":"To be engaged","description":"","type":"vimeo","additional_fields":{"vimeo-id":"66955509"},"id":"534a54326d30347963580000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/vimeo-66955509-438873348-640-1.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/vimeo-66955509-438873348-640-1.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/vimeo-66955509-438873348-640-1.jpg"}},"x":78,"y":1,"width":3,"height":2},{"title":"The tools","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>The tools (questions)</h1>"},"id":"534a546d6d30347966670000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":72,"y":1,"width":3,"height":2},{"title":"Discontinuity of ...","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<style>.set-in-stone{text-align:center;text-transform:uppercase;padding-bottom:0.5em;word-spacing:0.5em;}</style><h1 class=\"set-in-stone\">Discontinuity of continuity</h1><h1 class=\"set-in-stone\">Discontinuity of discontinuity</h1><h1 class=\"set-in-stone\">Continuity of discontinuity</h1>"},"id":"534a55306d30347963590000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":33,"y":1,"width":5,"height":4},{"title":"Concepts link","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"More concepts are explained in the <a href=\"#set/introduction-to-concepts\">\"Introduction to concepts\"</a> set"},"id":"534a572e6d303479635a0000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":75,"y":7,"width":4,"height":1},{"title":"Unfolding in the structure","description":"","type":"vimeo","additional_fields":{"vimeo-id":"67307273"},"id":"534a59036d303479635b0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/vimeo-67307273-439133684-640.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/vimeo-67307273-439133684-640.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/vimeo-67307273-439133684-640.jpg"}},"x":85,"y":4,"width":5,"height":4},{"title":"Time, space, ...","description":"","type":"vimeo","additional_fields":{"vimeo-id":"66955638"},"id":"534a596c6d303479635c0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/full/vimeo-66955638-438872570-640-1.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/small/vimeo-66955638-438872570-640-1.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/Cell/poster_image/medium/vimeo-66955638-438872570-640-1.jpg"}},"x":81,"y":4,"width":3,"height":2},{"title":"Structure text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>The structure is important, can it be revealed?</h1><p>We went for collecting <b>as many recordings as possible</b> to look out for variance and similarity between them.</p>"},"id":"534a59a76d30347966680000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":85,"y":1,"width":5,"height":3},{"title":"Recording setup text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>Recording setup</h1> <p>For Deborah Hay we had 3 recording sessions: February, April and October 2011. For the most part of Motion Bank phase 1 only the April 2011 data has been used so far: the 21 versions of Jeanine, Juliette and Ros. All recordings took place in Frankfurt (LAB Halle and TFC studios).</p> <p>One aim of Motion Bank was to develop methods that would allow smaller companies to redo the process we took. This means documentation, opening the tools (Instant Vision, Piecemaker) and using available and affordable technology (Full-HD camcorders).</p> <p>Another aspect was to minimize the amount of disturbance caused by the recording process. This was especially true for the dancers instrument: their body, and led to not using any body sensors or markers.</p>"},"id":"534a6bda6d30347966690000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":92,"y":1,"width":3,"height":7},{"title":"LAB recording setup","description":"","type":"image","additional_fields":{"image-src":"http://lab.motionbank.org/xyz.png","class":"hide-info"},"id":"534a6ca36d303479666c0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/full/Screen_Shot_2014-04-13_at_12.50.50_PM.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/small/Screen_Shot_2014-04-13_at_12.50.50_PM.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/medium/Screen_Shot_2014-04-13_at_12.50.50_PM.png"}},"x":96,"y":1,"width":8,"height":7},{"title":"Svenja explains computer vision approach ","description":"","type":"vimeo","additional_fields":{"vimeo-id":"78797665","autoload":"0","solo":"-1","attr-allowfullscreen":"allowfullscreen"},"id":"534a720b6d303479666d0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/full/454332916_640.jpg","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/small/454332916_640.jpg"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/medium/454332916_640.jpg"}},"x":105,"y":1,"width":6,"height":5},{"title":"Fraunhofer explain text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>Computer vision approach explained by Svenja Kahn from Fraunhofer IGD</h1>"},"id":"534a73b66d30347960530000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":105,"y":6,"width":4,"height":2},{"title":"Time synchronisation","description":"","type":"iframe","additional_fields":{"iframe-src":"https://lab.motionbank.org/jbmf/generators/pm_player_01/?vid=29163&gid=40&autoplay=0&loop=0","autoload":"0"},"id":"534a74ce6d303479635d0000","poster_image":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/full/Screen_Shot_2014-04-13_at_1.24.49_PM.png","small":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/small/Screen_Shot_2014-04-13_at_1.24.49_PM.png"},"medium":{"url":"/system/uploads/deborah_hay/GridCell/poster_image/medium/Screen_Shot_2014-04-13_at_1.24.49_PM.png"}},"x":112,"y":1,"width":6,"height":5},{"title":"Sync for PM text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>Embedding time into each device for later synchronisation in Piecemaker</h1>"},"id":"534a75236d30347960540000","poster_image":{"url":"/assets/fallback/default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png","small":{"url":"/assets/fallback/small_default-b553e49f4bf6795c93d62ecc6a576ac4.png"},"medium":{"url":"/assets/fallback/medium_default-cdee06016c3ca15e5810fcda0a4c5e44.png"}},"x":112,"y":6,"width":4,"height":2},{"title":"Manual markering text","description":"","type":"html","additional_fields":{"html-content":"<h1>The recordings were put into relation to the score text through manual markering in Piecemaker</h1><p><a href=\"https://vimeo.com/82728599\" target=\"_blank\">Introduction to the original Piecemaker 1</a> by David Kern, <a href=\"https://vimeo.com/album/2825847\" target=\"_blank\">more videos</a>, <a href=\"http://motionbank.org/en/event/pm2go-easy-use-video-annotation-tool\" target=\"_blan